    "data": {
      "title": "Digital Calendar Assembly",
      "topics": [],
      "fastest": false,
      "reverse": true,
      "shortest": true,
      "solution": "d, m, y = input().split()\nday1 = input()\n\n#parse the date\nleap = False if int(y)%4 or (int(y)%100==0 and int(y)%400) else True\nmth_days = 30 if m[:3] in ['Sep','Apr','Jun','Nov'] else 28 if m[0]=='F' and not leap else 29 if m[0]=='F' else 31\n\n#find start day position\nstart = ['Monday','Tuesday','Wednesday','Thursday','Friday','Saturday','Sunday'].index(day1)\n\n#fill calendar\ncal_days = [['  ' for i in range(7)] for j in range(6)]\nfor i in range(mth_days):\n    row, col = divmod(start+i,7)\n    day_num = f\"{i+1:02}\"\n    if day_num == d: cal_days[row][col] = 'XX' #mark current day\n    else: cal_days[row][col] = day_num\n\n#print top border\nprint('-'*22)\n#print year\nprint(f\"|{' '*15}{y} |\")\n#print month\nprint(f\"| {m}{' '*(19-len(m))}|\")\n#print empty line (with edge borders)\nprint(f\"|{' '*20}|\")\n#print days of week\nprint(\"|MO TU WE TH FR SA SU|\")\n#print separator line (dashes)\nprint(f\"|{'-'*20}|\")\n#print weeks of month\nfor i in cal_days: print(f\"|{' '.join(i)}|\")\n#print bottom border\nprint('-'*22)\n",
      "statement": "Given a [[date]] and the [[day]] that was or will be the {{1st}} of that [[Month]], build and print the calendar page for that [[Month]] with the given date [[DD]] marked {{XX}}.",
